        "color": "COLOR_WHITE",
        "postComment": "{\"data\":[{\"key\":\"C\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"A much more direct and energetic move than @@SANStart@@Ne5@@SANEnd@@. The most common response is @@SANStart@@dxe4@@SANEnd@@, which already concedes a comfortable opening advantage to White. The best move was played in this game, but Black will need to be well-prepared because the following move is not one that you can calculate at the board...\"},{\"key\":\"V\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":[{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"9.Ne5?!\"},{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"Bb7\"},{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"10.f4\"},{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"Ne7\"},{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"11.O-O\"},{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"Nf5\"},{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"12.Bf2\"},{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"Be7!\"},{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"13.g4\"},{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"Nd6\"},{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"14.g5\"},{\"key\":\"S\",\"state\":\"V\",\"val\":\"Nfe4\\u2a71\"},{\"state\":\"VV\",\"key\":\"C\",\"val\":\"This used to be the main line in this variation, and despite White's aggression on the kingside, it's clear that Black is the one who has benefited the most. When playing a stonewall structure in the London with @@SANStart@@f4@@SANEnd@@, it's crucial that we always maintain control of the @@SANStart@@e4@@SANEnd@@ square at all times. That has been completely forgotten in this position, and Black stands better with @@SANStart@@f6@@SANEnd@@ coming on the next move.\"}],\"line\":false}]}"
